\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{commit}{1c67513}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Three changes of evaluation need no switch because they change no result: a memo of 4,096 cells by term id for the values of closed nodes, an argument picker that returns the argument when the body of an application is a bound variable, and an immediate application record for a neutral head. Under the switch \code{\verb~|gated~} a depth rule was added: an inert application four or more inert levels below the root of its nest is always tabled. That removes a quadratic cliff of gated tabling on unshared dependent nests: a nest of 4,000 levels went from 8,038,031 ticks to 60,017.}

\p{Detail: [rep-machine-M2](rep-machine-M2), [design-switches-document](design-switches-document). Commit \commit{1c67513}. Session: [machine speed and pipeline](ses-CVTE). Related: [evaluation and tabling](design-evaluation-and-tabling).}
